    {
      "id": "p0191-b003",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Underta/e's English script sometimes uses the Japanese word tsundere. In broad terms, tsundere - roughly pronounced \"tsoon deh reh\" - describes the trait of having an unfriendly attitude on the outside that gives way to an affectionate inner attitude over time.",
        "raw": "Underta/e's English script sometimes uses the Japanese word tsundere. In\nbroad terms, tsundere - roughly pronounced \"tsoon deh reh\" - describes\nthe trait of having an unfriendly attitude on the outside that gives way to an\naffectionate inner attitude over time.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.09176591,
          0.23402857,
          0.67177167,
          0.301
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.0857453,
          0.23331429,
          0.70512442,
          0.30207143
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          16,
          19,
          21,
          22
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "《Undertale》的英文剧本偶尔会用日语词 tsundere（傲娇，读音大致是“tsoon deh reh”）。广义上，它形容一种性格：表面不友善，内心的亲昵却随着时间渐渐显露。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": [
