    {
      "id": "p0191-b004",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Twndere is a common word in Japanese entertainment, but is notoriously troublesome to translate into English because it has no solid equivalent. For this reason, English-speaking fans of Japanese entertainment - such as Toby - tend to leave the word untranslated. Basically, tsundere is in the process of becoming a loan word in English like \"karate\" and \"karaoke\", but it hasn't yet reached mainstream recognition. As such, the word tsundere might confuse some English-speaking players, but it poses little problem for Japanese players.",
        "raw": "Twndere is a common word in Japanese entertainment, but is notoriously\ntroublesome to translate into English because it has no solid equivalent. For\nthis reason, English-speaking fans of Japanese entertainment - such as Toby\n- tend to leave the word untranslated. Basically, tsundere is in the process of\nbecoming a loan word in English like \"karate\" and \"karaoke\", but it hasn't yet\nreached mainstream recognition. As such, the word tsundere might confuse\nsome English-speaking players, but it poses little problem for Japanese players.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.08778273,
          0.31594286,
          0.70308699,
          0.43853571
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.0857453,
          0.31522857,
          0.70512442,
          0.43960714
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          23,
          24,
          25,
          27,
          29,
          31,
          34
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "Tsundere 在日本娱乐作品中很常见，却因英语没有确切的对应词而出了名地难译。因此，像 Toby 这样的英语圈日本娱乐爱好者，通常直接保留原词。它正在像 karate（空手道）、karaoke（卡拉 OK）那样成为英语借词，但还没被主流广泛认识。所以它可能让一些英语玩家困惑，日本玩家却很容易理解。",
        "status": "draft",
